{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>If you will indeed heed the voice of YHWH your Elohim.</b> To accept upon yourself that statute which He has decreed for you, and from here onward <b>that which is upright in His eyes you shall do, and you shall hearken</b>, etc. — then you will be delivered from all the diseases of Egypt. But if you accept it now and afterward betray, He will visit upon you plague after plague without doubt. And this is like the matter of those of blessed memory: \"A gentile who comes to convert — they say to him: Know that before you came to this measure, if you ate fat you were not liable to karet; if you profaned the Sabbath you were not liable to stoning; but now, if you ate fat you are liable to karet,\" etc. (Yevamot 47a)." "<b>For I am YHWH your healer.</b> The reason that if you accept and afterward betray you will be punished, is that truly all My commandments are to heal your soul from the diseases of desires and corrupted dispositions, so that you may be holy to your Elohim, as it says: וָאַבְדִּיל אֶתְכֶם מִן הָעַמִּים לִהְיוֹת לִי (Leviticus 20:26). And if you betray, you wound and defile the soul, and it is fitting that one who defiles the holy thing of the Beloved be punished."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "Resolved כהנה וכהנה as 'plague after plague' based on the contextual threat of disease; the idiom means 'each and every plague.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:48.325978376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}